<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  cm_Relay_Config__c - where the execution relay lives, and the secret that proves the caller is us.

  PROTECTED, and a custom setting rather than a record or a constant, for three reasons:
    1. Protected visibility keeps it out of reports, list views and the API surface a subscriber
       or a curious user can browse. The secret is a bearer credential for a write door.
    2. Custom settings read out of the application cache, so the relay leg costs no SOQL query and
       no CRUD/FLS grant. The MCP dispatcher context is exactly the context that has least, and it
       still has to be able to read this.
    3. The URL and the secret move with the environment, not with the code. A sandbox refresh or a
       rotated secret is a data change, never a redeploy.

  Hierarchy type: one org-default row. Per-user relay endpoints would be a way to point a named
  user's writes somewhere else, which is precisely the thing this must not be able to do.

  The record itself is NEVER committed. It is inserted per-environment from the box that owns the
  secret (see /opt/connectry/c360-relay/.env, chmod 600).
-->
<CustomObject xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <customSettingsType>Hierarchy</customSettingsType>
    <description>Endpoint and shared secret for the Customer 360 execution relay. Read by ExecuteLoanModification when it runs in a context that cannot host nCino's credit-action engine.</description>
    <enableFeeds>false</enableFeeds>
    <label>C360 Relay Config</label>
    <visibility>Protected</visibility>
</CustomObject>
